@inherits LayoutComponentBase
@using BlazorAtoms.Breadcrumbs

@*
    The single site-chrome layout for all three demo hosts (Server / Auto / Wasm), merged here
    2026-08-27 the same way NavMenu was in July. It had drifted three ways: Svr had grown a second
    <AtomBreadcrumbBar /> inside its top-row plus an id="top-row" and a commented-out debug div,
    and only Svr carried the scroll-containment CSS (keyed off an id="content" the other two never
    had), so a scrolling fix had to be written twice before this merge.

    No #blazor-error-ui here. It belongs in each host's own host page — Components/App.razor for
    Svr and Auto, wwwroot/index.html for standalone Wasm — with its styles in that app's unscoped
    wwwroot/app.css. That is where the Blazor templates put it, and the reason is real: the banner
    has to be able to appear for failures that happen before this layout has ever rendered.

    Scoped CSS in an RCL is fine — the SDK folds Demos.Shared's .razor.css into each consuming
    app's <App>.styles.css bundle, exactly as it already does for NavMenu.razor.css.
*@
<style>
    main {
        min-width: 0px;
        flex: 1 1 0%;
    }

    article {
        max-width: 100%;
        box-sizing: border-box;
    }
</style>
<div class="page">
    <div class="sidebar">
        <NavMenu />
    </div>

    <main>
        <div class="top-row px-4">
            <a href="about">About</a>
        </div>

        <div class="px-4">
            <AtomBreadcrumbBar />
        </div>

        <article class="content px-4">
            @Body
        </article>
    </main>
</div>
